# One line per backup job. Times are UTC.
#
# A job is `backup-postgres <name>` (a database) or `backup-storage <name>`
# (the files of a Supabase Storage service). Its settings come from the
# environment as BACKUP_<NAME>_* (see compose.yaml, compose.supabase.yaml and
# .env.example), and its files land under <name>/ in the bucket. Output goes
# to the container log.
#
# A job whose settings are not there is not scheduled: the container says so
# when it starts. That is how the two Supabase jobs stay off until
# compose.supabase.yaml is switched on (README.md).
#
# To add a job: add a line here, add its BACKUP_<NAME>_* block to a compose
# file and .env, attach the container to that database's network, then
# `sudo docker compose up -d --build`.

# min hour day month weekday  command

# Inngest's Postgres, nightly.
17 7 * * * backup-postgres inngest >/proc/1/fd/1 2>&1

# The app's own database (Supabase), every hour. 48 hourly and 30 daily kept.
43 * * * * backup-postgres supabase >/proc/1/fd/1 2>&1

# The app's stored files (Supabase Storage), nightly.
27 7 * * * backup-storage supabase-storage >/proc/1/fd/1 2>&1
